[Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  we've all heard of formula one race cars  but how about  formula e this weekend all electric cars  will compete in new york at speeds of up  to 174 miles an hour  it comes after every major car maker  announced plans this year  to go electric several fully by 2035.  some of the technology we're seeing in  the competition could end up in your  neighborhood  errol barnett is at the racetrack in  brooklyn errol good morning  hey there good morning consider this 10  years ago this sport didn't even  exist now what's known as the e pre  boasts 12 teams 24  drivers speeding across at least three  continents this season  and growing it is high energy meets high  tech  and i can tell you that come rain or  shine this weekend these races  are on coming down into the new nouvelle  chicane  de costa to the outside it's a  country-hopping heart-stopping racing  tournament for the 21st century  coming up through beau rivage they're  still three wide electric racing cars  earning fans by burning rubber brilliant  drive from mortara  do you see any other team as your  biggest threat or is everybody a threat  the beauty  of former e is it's so close every team  is a threat  susie wolf is team principal for rocket  venturi racing  fresh off a win in pueblo mexico last  month vaulting her driver edo mottara to  the top  of the driver standings this is one of  our cars getting unpacked the tournament  though  is far from over it's brutal there's  only ever one winner and everybody wants  to win  but sport is also so pure you know  exactly how good you're doing  based on your own track results the  chequered flag falls currently leading  the team standings is mercedes  the electric mobility age is upon us  team principal ian james who worked for  a time at the mercedes plant in  tuscaloosa alabama says what happens  here  can end up in your driveway if you think  about electric mobility there are  certain challenges which come up for the  engineers  ultimately it's how efficient you can  actually make that power unit and the  cars themselves  we can hopefully prove our  competitiveness here that then  translates auto and  also into the road car side of things  what makes formula e racing unique is  that each vehicle is equipped with the  same electric battery and a fixed range  the current version is called gen 2 with  a top speed  of 174 miles per hour how each team  uses that power while conserving energy  makes all the difference  the car from the front to here is the  same for everybody  and from here to the back this is where  they are developing something  fred espinos says teams never reveal  what's under their casings for risk of  exposing  engineering secrets so he showed us  inside a standard race car and showed  what the soon to be released  gen 3 battery will do what will be  different in the new car  is that there will be a second power  trend which will be at the front of the  car  wow and the second power trend will be  there to help the car to go faster at  the start  this temporary race track in brooklyn  feels more like a travelling carnival of  cutting-edge racing technology  the sky's the limit alberto longo  co-founded formula e in 2013 to create a  sport  focused on sustainability we're going to  have  flash charging which is basically going  to be able to charge the car  within the course of 30 seconds but it  does have its fair share of detractors  specifically over the power boost using  fan boost he got to the outside  the game-like concept allows fans to  vote for their favorite driver during a  race  those drivers with the five highest  tallies then get extra acceleration  in a specially marked zone what do you  say to people who say  this feels like a video game you take  that as a compliment or not  i do actually because this is the  intention out of the final corner now  and he is a two times formulary champion  now longo admits his sport does suffer  from a visible lack of diversity he  suggests for every thousand boys there's  maybe a single girl that wants to get  into racing  so motorsports governing body has an  initiative called girls on track  aiming to make all of this all of what  you've seen here more accessible jamie  to young women that's a great idea start  your engine it's going to sound a little  different too errol thank you  you can watch formula e tomorrow at 4 pm  eastern on cbs sports network and sunday  at 1 pm eastern here on cbs  we'll be right back

